{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Can a single batch be split across multiple vats (processed in parallel on more than one vat at a time), or must each batch be assigned to exactly one vat for its entire processing?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding batch assignment, which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When you say each batch must go through the vats in the order first, second, then third, does the processing time for a batch on a given vat come from that vat's column in the matrix (i.e., batch i takes p[i][j] on vat j, so batch 1 takes 3 on vat 1, 1 on vat 2, 1 on vat 3)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of the mapping between batches, vats, and the processing time matrix."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there any setup or changeover time between consecutive batches on the same vat, or can a vat start the next batch immediately once the previous one finishes?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the existence of setup time or the ability to start immediately, which constitutes one independent policy choice."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since setup time is still being confirmed, should I model the vats as having zero setup time between batches (so a vat can start the next batch the instant the previous one finishes)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a specific modeling assumption regarding setup time."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there any limit on how many batches can be waiting in the queue between vats (for example, a maximum number of batches that can be finished on vat 1 but not yet started on vat 2), or is the queue between vats unlimited?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the capacity limit of the queue between vats."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Can a batch start on vat 2 the moment it finishes on vat 1, even if other batches are still being processed on vat 1 (i.e., is there no restriction that a vat must finish all its current work before the next vat can take a batch)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking about the scheduling constraint for batch transfer between vats. Although it includes a parenthetical explanation, it seeks a single policy confirmation."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Do all 5 batches start available at time 0, or do some batches have release times (earliest start times) that are later than 0?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the availability timing of the batches."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is the objective to minimize the time at which the last batch finishes on vat 3 (the final stage), i.e., the makespan of the whole flow shop?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of the optimization objective."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 2,
  "is_atomic": false,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are the processing times in the matrix in the same units as the makespan you want to minimize (e.g., all in hours)?",
    "Should the answer be reported in those same units?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains two semantically independent questions: one asking about the consistency of units between input data and the objective, and another asking about the required units for the final report. A user could confirm the first without necessarily confirming the second, or vice versa."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Can a vat process at most one batch at a time (i.e., no two batches on the same vat overlap in time)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking about the capacity constraint of a vat, with no other independent questions or stop signals."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the several points still under internal confirmation (setup time, queue limits, release times, units, and whether a vat can run two batches at once), should I proceed with the standard flow-shop assumptions — zero setup, unlimited queue, all batches available at time 0, times in the same units as the matrix, and one batch per vat at a time — so that I can build the model now?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single yes/no question about whether to proceed with a specific set of default assumptions, treating the list of parameters as a single bundle for one decision."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "If I must proceed without confirmation on the open points, should I assume the standard flow-shop setup where each vat processes at most one batch at a time, with no setup time, no release times, and an unlimited queue between vats?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy decision: whether to assume a specific set of standard flow-shop constraints. Although multiple constraints are listed, they form a single coherent assumption package that requires one yes/no answer."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Should I go ahead and build the model now using the standard flow-shop assumptions (one batch per vat at a time, zero setup, all batches available at time 0, unlimited queue between vats), and flag those assumptions clearly in the final model so they can be adjusted once your team confirms them?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single compound request asking for permission to proceed with a specific set of assumptions and a specific documentation method. Since the user must provide a single yes/no decision to authorize this combined action, it counts as one semantically independent question."
}

